    "catalog:attribution": "Vishwajeet Mane",
    "catalog:category": "sanitary",
    "catalog:placement": "free",
    "catalog:lod": "300",
    "catalog:tags": "basin, wash basin, pedestal, bathroom",
    "catalog:note": "Pedestal wash basin against the wall. rim 0.85. A rim slab 0.04 thick with rounded front corners over a bowl body of the same D as the bowl, both drawn as pairs of straight sweeps with a round bowl of radius 0.15 through them; a bowl floor closes it 0.13 below the rim. The pedestal runs from the wall to under the bowl and hides the trap and the supplies. Parts under radius 0.04 build as polygonal prisms at true size.",
    "catalog:basedOn": "Drafting standard key dimensions (practice, Neufert / Metric Handbook), unverified: wash basin 0.55 x 0.45, rim 0.85; EN 14688 not read. Bowl depth 0.13 and the body sizes are the author's, unverified. Port sizes from the drafting standard (BS EN 12056-2 conventions), unverified",
    "ifc:class": "IfcSanitaryTerminal",
    "ifc:predefinedType": "WASHHANDBASIN",
    "ifcClass": "IfcSanitaryTerminal",
